new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b35c35c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ms58-extension-profile.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Experimental extension profiling
+
+This diagnostic derivative starts from integrated Kayros `327e481713e1b9a3187fda2fc9f10f8d9d75b0c5`. It preserves the canonical valuation changes, scalar-point CHOICE repair, arithmetic gates, feasibility predicates, cut updates and normalization. No solver experiment has been launched from this worktree. We use the diagnostic to identify where extension spends time before proposing another optimization.
+
+The CMake option `KAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILING` defaults to `OFF`. When disabled, both labeling translation units have the same preprocessed content as the base after whitespace removal. When enabled, the definition is public on the `lera` target so its bridge sees the same class layouts. It does not reach the independent `_core` target or its ILS implementation. All profile counters, timers and file ownership belong to one `BidirectionalLabeling` object. No mutable global or thread-local profile state is introduced.
+
+## Activation and identity
+
+Build a fresh CPLEX diagnostic variant with `-DKAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILING=ON` in addition to the existing CMake settings. The runtime variable `KAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILE` must name a new JSONL file. Creation is exclusive, so a second solve must use a different path. Missing runtime opt-in leaves the diagnostic inactive. The compiled diagnostic variant must still be kept separate from timing builds, even when the runtime variable is unset.
+
+The optional variables `KAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILE_STRIDE` and `KAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILE_OFFSET` select deterministic samples. Their defaults are `1009` and `0`. Each direction samples zero-based extension attempts whose ordinal modulo stride equals offset, resetting at each pricing task. Invalid settings fail before opening the output. The opening record identifies schema `kayros-ms58-extension-profile-v1`, the base source, sample rule and clock. The run manifest must additionally retain the complete derivative commit, patch, binary, input and harness hashes.
+
+Every task writes a flushed `pricing_begin` containing the complete pricing problem and effective labeling flags. It then writes cumulative `pricing_progress` records at most once per 5 seconds, checked after sampled extensions and monodirectional batches. A single long operation can delay a progress record. Normal return writes `pricing_end` with the unchanged native log, returned-route count and pool size. `pricing_returned=true` means only that the pricing method returned. The native log distinguishes time limits, memory limits, solution limits and finished pricing. A begin without an end remains unfinished, including after exceptions or process termination. No record asserts solver closure or proof validity.
+
+## Measurements
+
+Every extension attempt contributes counters, including attempts that return no label. Each direction records rejection reasons, the before-window/legacy/step branches, normalization fast returns and rebuilds, NG/full visited sets, strong/weak unreachable updates and returned labels. These counters cover only `ExtensionStep`, so normalization performed by dominance or correction is outside this profile.
+
+Sampled attempts partition extension wall time across feasibility checks, label allocation and scalar resources, arithmetic gating, before-window evaluation, PWL addition, PWL subtraction, PWL composition, domain restriction, normalization, visited sets, unreachable calculation, cut resources and final scalar/trace work. The unreachable stage excludes the surrounding set union. Nested stage timers are exclusive. A stage's entry count includes resumption after nested work and must not be read as an operator invocation count. The step path's final addition stage also includes its existing empty-result check and copy branch. The domain-restriction call remains exactly as implemented, including its discarded return value.
+
+The addition/subtraction result is passed by forwarding reference into `Compose`. This retains the original full expression, arithmetic order and temporary lifetime. No PWL operators, CHOICE/JUMP semantics or normalizer rules are changed. Sampled piece statistics report count, sum and maximum for parent duration, arc travel, arc departure, the precomposition arithmetic result, the composed result and the normalized duration. They use `PieceCount()` and do not rescan function pieces.
+
+The stage times include clock and bookkeeping overhead. The rare JSON write happens after the sampled episode timer stops, but it remains inside the native extension timer when triggered from an extension. Sampling can correlate with search order, so an offset repeat is useful if a proposed mechanism depends on a narrow class of labels. These are diagnostic wall-time samples, without extrapolated CPU attribution or a solver throughput claim. Compare ordered route pools and native work counts against the uninstrumented base before interpreting stage proportions. Sample size and piece statistics must accompany those proportions.
+
+## Validation and next runs
+
+The standalone fixture `tests/cpp/test_extension_profile.cpp` passes sampling, direction separation, task reset, exclusive stage accounting, nested-call evaluation counts, original temporary lifetime, unchanged native status, unfinished-task handling, exclusive output creation and invalid-setting checks. It does not invoke the solver or an LP backend. The compile-on labeling source also passes a C++23 syntax check in the project development shell.
+
+The native fixture `tests/cpp/test_extension_profile_pwl.cpp` supplies 384 bitwise comparisons of the original and wrapped PWL expressions across both arithmetic modes, full and point domains, stacked CHOICE and JUMP pieces, sampled and unsampled attempts. Compile and execute it against the newly built diagnostic `liblera.a` on reserved compute before the first solver run. Its execution is pending. A matching expression fixture does not establish full solver trajectory equivalence.
+
+```bash
+g++ -std=c++23 -O2 -DNDEBUG -ffp-contract=off \
+  -DKAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILING=1 \
+  -Icpp/lera/main/include -Icpp/lera/goc/include \
+  tests/cpp/test_extension_profile.cpp \
+  -o build/ms58/test_extension_profile
+build/ms58/test_extension_profile
+
+g++ -std=c++23 -O2 -DNDEBUG -ffp-contract=off \
+  -DKAYROS_EXTENSION_PROFILING=1 \
+  -Icpp/lera/main/include -Icpp/lera/goc/include \
+  tests/cpp/test_extension_profile_pwl.cpp \
+  build/cplex/cpp/lera/liblera.a -ldl -lm \
+  -o build/ms58/test_extension_profile_pwl
+build/ms58/test_extension_profile_pwl
+```
+
+All new comparative solver pilots must use Dabia2013 instances with 25, 50 or 100 customers and CPLEX, and include minimally corrected Lera `f2c9e20`. The direct diagnostic control is uninstrumented best `327e481`. Start with the C104 workload that motivated the profile, retain unfinished records and compare completed-task work signatures before interpreting cost by stage. Any promotion or speed measurement belongs in a separate build with profiling disabled. This patch does not combine with the dominance-scratch candidate.
